Pine v6 structured signature + behavior data
=============================================

Source:  https://github.com/folknor/pine-tools, pine-data/v6/*.json
License: MIT (folknor owns pine-tools)

Files in this directory are point-in-time snapshots of pine-tools'
data-pipeline output (`pnpm run scrape`). They originate from crawling and
parsing TradingView's published Pine v6 documentation; trademarks belong to
TradingView.

Files:
  - functions.json    (475 entries) signatures, params, flags, overloads, examples
  - variables.json    (162 entries) built-in variables (close, high, time)
  - constants.json    (237 entries) constants (color.red, shape.circle)
  - keywords.json      (30 entries)  reserved keywords (objects: description + prose sub-sections)
  - types.json         (20 entries)  built-in types (chart.point, line, array, ...)
  - annotations.json   (10 entries)  compiler annotations (@version=, @param, ...)
  - operators.json     (21 entries)  operators (+, -, ?:, [], +=, ...)

Schema notes:
  - functions.json `flags` now carries the full polymorphism surface
    (`polymorphic` = "input" | "element" | "numeric", plus `returnTypeParam`).
    The previously-separate function-behavior.json was retired upstream when
    polymorphism was consolidated into these flags; it is no longer vendored.
  - Per-parameter `default`, `allowedValues`, `min`, and `max` and a top-level
    `overloads[]` array (per-overload signatures) are newer fields; the binary
    surfaces them in `po lookup` and BM25 search.
  - Parameters (and overload parameters) carry two newer lint-oriented fields:
    `expectedTypeNoun` (the single concrete type a union-typed parameter such as
    "series int/float" actually expects) and `rangeSource` ("reference" when the
    min/max came from TV's published docs, "runtime" when it was observed from
    the compiler). The binary deserializes leniently and does not render either.
  - Every catalog now carries the prose sub-sections `remarks`, `seeAlso`, and
    `returnsDescription` (the "Returns" sentence, distinct from the typed
    return) where TV documents them. These let `po lookup` render the full
    reference card straight from pine-data; the markdown reference vendor was
    retired once they landed.

Snapshot: pine-tools scrape 2026-09-07 (pine-tools ab72479, "Validate UDT field
defaults"). Changes vs. 2026-08-15:
  - keywords.json: 28 -> 30 entries. `once` (the new single-execution
    conditional structure) and `for...in` are now documented as keywords; the
    latter was previously hidden by a crawler bug fixed upstream in dfa6c6d.
  - functions.json: 140 entries changed, all of them parameter-level metadata
    additions - `expectedTypeNoun` on union-typed parameters, and `rangeSource`
    plus a few runtime-observed `min` bounds (e.g. `ta.pivothigh`'s `leftbars`).
    No whitespace-only churn.
  - functions.json: `math.avg`, `math.sign`, and `math.sum` lost
    `flags.polymorphic = "numeric"`; the classification now applies only to
    `math.abs`, `math.max`, and `math.min`.
  - The other five catalogs are byte-identical to 2026-08-15.
The JSON files are bare arrays with no embedded generation timestamp; the
snapshot date above is baked into the binary as behavior::PINE_DATA_SNAPSHOT for
`po version`.

Refresh procedure: re-run pine-tools' data pipeline (`pnpm run scrape`), copy
the resulting JSON files in, update the counts / snapshot ref above and the
PINE_DATA_SNAPSHOT constant in src/behavior/core.rs, then commit with a note
about which scrape revision is current.
